{"raw": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492866/assistant-professor-of-english": {"title": "Assistant Professor of English", "description": "Assistant Professor of English Salary $60,000.00 - $63,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC983-1 Division College of Humanities & Social Sciences Department English Opening Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of English at Utah Tech University (UT), in the picturesque red-rock southwestern city of St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of English, with an emphasis in Rhetoric and Composition and specializing in interdisciplinary writing, to begin July 1, 2027. We are particularly interested in candidates who draw upon their doctoral emphases to collaborate with disciplines across the university (specifically STEM, Business, Education, Health Sciences, and the Arts) in both lower-division composition courses and our upper-division course offerings. Furthermore, candidates will have an interest and/or expertise in emerging technologies, including AI and emergent multimodal software with a focus on professional development. The English department offers associate and bachelor\u2019s degrees in English with emphases in Creative Writing, English Education, Literary Studies, and Professional and Technical Writing, as well as minors in Creative Writing, English Education, General Education, and Professional and Technical Writing. The English Department also offers a Masters of Arts in Technical Writing and Digital Rhetoric. Utah Tech is an open-enrollment institution, and the English department provides the university with traditional General Education composition courses as well as corequisite and developmental reading and writing courses designed to help at-risk students succeed. Additional information about the English department, its faculty, and programs is found online at https://english.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 semester hours in lower division, upper division, and graduate-level English courses\u2014including traditional composition, corequisite composition, and developmental reading and writing\u2014as needed by the department. Teach lower division and upper division courses in Rhetoric and Composition. Lead department efforts in fostering interdisciplinary relationships across campus and developing interdisciplinary curriculum for composition courses with a focus on emerging technologies. Engage in scholarship relevant to the position at a level appropriate to a teaching university (both scholarship of discovery and scholarship of pedagogy are valued at UT). Assist in curriculum creation in Rhetoric and Composition. Serve on departmental, college, and university committees as assigned and attend departmental, college, and university meetings as required. Work with the department chair, the dean, and other faculty to advance the university\u2019s mission, including: Work constructively, collaboratively, and collegially with faculty and staff in the department and across campus. Conduct student assessment. Hold regular office hours. Mentor part-time instructors. Perform service for the college and university. Participate in university and departmental student recruitment and retention initiatives. Facilitate service learning and engagement with the community. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Ph.D. or Ed.D. in English, Rhetoric and Composition (or related field) by August 2027 from a regionally accredited institution required. A demonstrated record of teaching, service, and scholarship in Rhetoric and Composition, interdisciplinary writing, and emerging technologies. Evidence of university-wide and professional networking Ability to analyze and employ various communication and teaching technologies. Ability to communicate clearly with students, staff and colleagues, both orally and in writing. An eagerness to engage with faculty, staff and administrators to develop ways to improve the educational experience of students. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $60,000-$63,000,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 26, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Ph.D. or Ed.D. in English, Rhetoric and Composition (or related field) by August 2027 from a regionally accredited institution, as required in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492917/assistant-professor-of-psychology-marriage-and-family-therapy": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology - Marriage and Family Therapy", "description": "Assistant Professor of Psychology - Marriage and Family Therapy Salary $75,500.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC812-1 Division College of Humanities & Social Sciences Department Psychology Opening Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Marriage and Family Therapy Master\u2019s program in the Psychology Department at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, invites applications for 2 full-time, 10-month, tenure-track positions as an Assistant Professor of Marriage and Family Therapy, with a projected start date of January 1, 2027,or July 1, 2027 or until filled. The preferred candidate will possess a terminal degree in MFT and be licensed or license-eligible in the State of Utah. Teaching responsibilities will include both graduate and undergraduate courses, with primary responsibilities within the MFT Master\u2019s program. The Marriage and Family Therapy (MFT) Program at Utah Tech University is a growing graduate program within the Department of Psychology dedicated to preparing students to serve others as practicing marriage and family therapists. Through a combination of rigorous academic training, diverse clinical experiences, research opportunities, and attentive supervision, the program develops culturally competent, ethical, and effective clinicians who make meaningful contributions to the profession and their communities. Emphasizing systemic theory, evidence-based practice, and hands-on clinical training, the program prepares students to work with individuals, couples, and families while meeting the educational and supervised clinical experience requirements for licensure in Utah. Consistent with Utah Tech University's mission, the program is committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and student success. The MFT program continues to grow and seeks faculty who are dedicated to high-quality graduate education, student mentorship, and advancing the field of marriage and family therapy. More information about the program can be found online at https://psychology.utahtech.edu/mft/ . The Psychology department and its programs are situated in a new, 120,000 square foot building on the UT campus with dedicated space for a community mental health clinic. UT is a regional, comprehensive university with an \u201copen, inclusive, comprehensive, polytechnic\u201d mission. The Psychology Department, including the MFT program, plays an important role in fulfilling the university\u2019s mission. UT is particularly welcoming to active learning modalities in our coursework. Similarly, we encourage and value faculty scholarship that involves student researchers, as well as scholarship that informs the faculty member\u2019s teaching. Responsibilities This full-time, tenure-track position involves teaching responsibilities related to the faculty member\u2019s expertise in both the undergraduate and graduate programs, along with service and scholarship commensurate with the expectations of a faculty member at a teaching university like UT. The specific expectations for the successful candidate will be to: Teach 24 credit hours of courses each academic year, consisting of courses within the undergraduate psychology program and graduate MFT program as well as one graduate course during the summer. Course assignments will be made by the Department Chair in consultation with the MFT Program Director, to address departmental needs and the expertise of faculty. Course assignments will include: Undergraduate courses such as Abnormal Psychology and Introduction to Marriage and Family Therapy Graduate courses such as play therapy, gender and culture, working with families with children, MFT Theories, and practicum Participate in teaching and learning seminars and activities designed to promote and develop instructional knowledge and skills Attend department, division, and college faculty meetings, and work with other faculty and staff in improving the overall education experience of Psychology majors and MFT graduate students Engage in scholarship and/or creative activity appropriate to a teaching university. UT values both scholarship of discovery and scholarship of pedagogy within the context of our teaching mission (clinical work associated with mental health therapy is an accepted form of scholarly engagement when accompanied by other scholarly production such as conference presentations or publications) Create programing and scholarship that facilitates growth towards Utah Tech becoming an accredited program Facilitate the development and growth of a Utah Tech community clinic, supporting both developing therapists as well as support the community with mental health care Supervise student internship experiences (for both graduate and undergraduate students), helping students integrate evidence-based academic concepts with practical internship experience, including support at the UT Community Health Clinic Participate in service activities, including on department, college, or university committees including work towards accreditation for Utah Tech Maintain a scholarly agenda that is appropriate to a teaching university like Utah Tech community. Qualifications Doctoral degree in Marriage and Family Therapy from an accredited college or university required. ABD may be considered if degree is awarded prior to July 2027 Evidence of potential for successful teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal skills An eagerness to engage with colleagues, staff, administrators, and community organizations to develop ways to improve the educational experience for our students Licensed or able to get licensure in the state of Utah as an MFT Is or can become an AAMFT approved supervisor prior to hire date Emphasis in child and adolescent treatment preferred relations. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (10-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits starting January 2, 2027, or July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $75,500 with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 26, 2026 ; position open until filled.? Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Doctoral degree in Marriage and Family Therapy from an accredited college or university as indicated in the job posting? ABD may be considered if degree is awarded prior to July 2027. Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492976/resident-life-area-coordinator": {"title": "Resident Life Area Coordinator", "description": "Resident Life Area Coordinator Salary $44,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 27PRO760-1 Division Student Affairs Department Auxiliary Housing Opening Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement Responsible for coordinating the day-to-day operation and programs of Campus View Suites 1, averaging 352 residents, the University Inn, averaging 44 residents, and Family Student Housing, averaging 21 apartments. This involves overseeing development of a community and educational environment that encourages student engagement, positive relationships, and student success. In addition to traditional residence life functions and roles, this position will have specific responsibilities regarding student conduct and student staff development across all on campus residential communities. This position is required to live in provided on-campus housing within Campus View Suites 1. Information about Housing and Resident Life can be found online at https://housing.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Coordinate the day-to-day resident life operations and programs of Campus View Suites 1, the University Inn, and Family Student Housing apartments. Assist in the management and facilitation of the student conduct process by implementing and enforcing university and departmental rules and regulations, as well as adjudicating minor student conduct cases, across all residence halls (approximately 1,600 residents) as assigned by the Assistant Director and Director. Plan and organize for summer camps and conferences, including occupancy management in coordination with campus partners, staff selection and training, cleaning checks, key preparation and management, and invoicing. Oversee the development of a community and educational environment that encourages student engagement, positive relationships, and student success. Respond to emergency situations and assist in resolving resident and parent concerns, roommate conflict, etc. Plan and implement active educational, social and cultural programs for the personal growth and development of residents. Plan, propose, implement and assess Themed Communities, as determined by the department\u2019s strategic plan. Utilize StarRez (student housing management software) when performing daily responsibilities, including updating student and building information, processing forms, and creating reports. Participate in on-call duty coverage, one week out of every six weeks, to respond to on-campus student housing incidents and student crisis situations. Monitor and communicate concerns related to facilities, including safety and security, cleaning service, maintenance and keys. Provide supervision and assistance during check-in/check-out periods. Plan, organize, and assist in the facilitation of the centralized process for resident assistant and resident manager recruitment, selection, placement and training. Supervise 9 Resident Assistants and 2 Assistant Resident Managers. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Any combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis. Master\u2019s degree preferred. Two years\u2019 experience working in Residence Life, Student Involvement, or related fields during graduate or undergraduate career required. Experience advising a student group preferred. The total qualifications required are based on a combination of education and work experience. Any experience used to meet the education requirement cannot also be used to meet the work experience requirement. Knowledge of Student Development and Student Involvement theories required; knowledge and experience with Living Learning Communities preferred. Computer proficiency, with good knowledge of Microsoft Office suite (particularly Word and Outlook) required; knowledge of Banner, StarRez and Maxient systems preferred. Strong organizational skills, with ability to respond to, and concentrate on, multiple projects simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal interpersonal skills required, with the ability to interact with a diverse group of individuals and campus departments in establishing and maintaining effective and positive relationships. Outgoing personality, with a history of dependability, reliability, and initiative. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time professional staff (overtime-exempt) position. Annual salary of $44,000 with rent and utility free two-bedroom and one bath apartment provided. Desired start date of November 2026. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, as well as paid holidays in addition to sick and vacation leave accruals. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026; position open until filled . Submit application materials (including resume contents and contact information for three professional references) and upload a cover letter electronically. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY:? Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success 