pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. Cover Letter Resume Contact information (including email) for three professional references Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold at least a Bachelor's degree in the required area for this position by the desired start date? A combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis. Yes No 03 Do you currently have at least two years of experience as listed in the job announcement? The total qualifications required are based on a combination of education and work experience. Any experience used to meet the education requirement cannot also be used to meet the work experience requirement. Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5497731/executive-director-of-business-services": {"title": "Executive Director of Business Services", "description": "Executive Director of Business Services Salary See Position Description Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 27PRO767-2 Division Administrative Affairs Department Business Services Opening Date 09/28/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Announcement The Executive Director of Business Services serves as the institution\u2019s Treasurer and provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the University\u2019s core financial operations, including accounting, financial reporting, accounts payable, accounts receivable, treasury operations, and related compliance functions. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Business and Auxiliary Services, this position ensures the integrity, accuracy, and transparency of the University\u2019s financial records and internal control environment. The position leads continuous process improvement initiatives, supports enterprise-wide financial systems, and collaborates across campus to advance the University\u2019s mission and strategic goals. Additional information about the department can be found online at https://employees.utahtech.edu/business-services/ . Responsibilities Provide leadership and direct supervision for accounting, student finance, accounts payable, accounts receivable, fixed assets, and financial reporting functions. Oversee treasury-related activities including cash management, banking relationships, and liquidity monitoring. Provide accounting support and direction to the University\u2019s Foundation(s). Coordinate and prepare annual financial statements in accordance with GAAP and GASB standards. Lead fiscal year-end close processes and coordinate external audit activities. Ensure integrity and governance of the University\u2019s chart of accounts and financial approval workflows, and records retention. Develop, implement, and maintain strong internal controls and financial policies and procedures. Ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations and reporting requirements. Provide leadership in implementation, optimization, and maintenance of enterprise financial systems (e.g., ERP platforms such as Ellucian Banner). Develop and mentor high-performing teams; foster a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Provide training and guidance to campus budget officers and departments regarding financial policies, procedures, and systems. Serve on institutional committees and represent Business Services in campus-wide initiatives. Serves as the second-in-command and primary backup to the Assistant Vice President (AVP), providing leadership support, overseeing operations in the AVP\u2019s absence, and ensuring continuity of departmental functions and responsibilities. Perform other duties as assigned in support of institutional objectives. Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in accounting, as well as Masters of Accountancy or closely-related degree, required. CPA certification preferred. Any combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis. CPA certification or willingness to pursue CPA certification. At least five (5) years' direct accounting experience, with progressively higher levels of responsibility including team leadership, required. Experience in higher education accounting is preferred. The total qualifications required are based on a combination of education and work experience. Any experience used to meet the education requirement cannot also be used to meet the work experience requirement. Extensive knowledge in the use of Microsoft office products, in particular Excel and Access. Extensive experience in the use of Banner and Banner Modules, including FR, AP, AR, and Fixed Assets, or equivalent systems. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. An eagerness to engage with colleagues, to develop ways to improve the Business office policies and procedures. Good knowledge of accounting rules and regulations as they apply to higher education. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time overtime-exempt staff position. Annual salary of $120,000+, with a desired start date of January 2027. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, as well as paid holidays in addition to sick and vacation leave accruals. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026; position open until filled . Submit application materials (including resume contents and contact information for three professional references) and upload a cover letter electronically. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5499980/assistant-professor-of-communication": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Communication", "description": "Assistant Professor of Communication Salary $58,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC904-1 Division College of Humanities & Social Sciences Department Communication Opening Date 09/30/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Communication at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, is seeking one creative and passionate teacher/scholar for a tenure-track position of Assistant Professor of Communication, with an emphasis in Leadership and Organizational Communication, to begin Fall 2027 semester. The position requires a 4/4 teaching load per academic year, and the successful candidates will be expected to teach courses related to student leadership, organizational communication, and/or professional communication. We invite applicants who teach and develop research on leadership and organizational communication across theoretical and paradigmatic approaches (qualitative, critical, quantitative), with interest areas in including, but not limited to, compassionate leadership, student-led organizing, community leadership and organizing, organizational support, ethics in leadership, public relations, strategic communication (across local/global contexts), and organizational justice and activism . Special consideration will be given to the applicant with a strong commitment to student mentorship and success. Special consideration will also be given to the applicant with a with a desire to reinvigorate the department\u2019s current curriculum and design new courses related to the candidate\u2019s specialty area(s). The primary consideration for tenure at UT is teaching, with expectations of university- and college-level service beginning at the second year of employment. Maintaining an active research trajectory is highly desired. Utah Tech University is establishing itself as a regional, comprehensive university with an \u201copen, inclusive, comprehensive, polytechnic\u201d mission and the Communication Department plays an important role in fulfilling the university\u2019s mission. More information about the department and its programs can be found online at https://communication.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 credits per academic year (with potential for overload) in Communication. Course assignments include Leadership and Performance Teams, Organizational Communication and System Dynamics, Professional Relationships, Persuasion, and Ethics in Communication as well as introductory communication courses within the department curriculum. Provide regular institutional service as outlined in Regent and University policy. Consult with department chair and college dean in creating and proposing new curriculum. Work with other faculty in program management, including furthering development and campus promotion of the Communication field, department, and programs. Adhere to department, college, and university policies and perform campus-wide faculty responsibilities. Develop and maintain a scholarship agenda in area of expertise that is appropriate to a teaching university like Utah Tech. Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. in Communication or related field required. A specialty that addresses the intersection of leadership and organizational communication is highly desired. ABD may be considered if completion of degree will occur by July 1, 2027. Have experience teaching and/or designing courses related to organizational communication, professional communication, leadership, and other core communication classes such as communication theory and research. Demonstrate excellence or potential in instructing college-level courses, utilizing a variety of teaching techniques and strategies. Demonstrate willingness to participate in college and departmental student recruitment and retention initiatives. Have experience in curriculum development. Ability to collaborate in a collegial, team-oriented workplace. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Sufficient experience in teaching, and working with, students with diverse educational and socioeconomic backgrounds. Demonstrate willingness to integrate active learning and other innovative pedagogical approaches in the classroom (see the University\u2019s \u201cactive learning, active life\u201d mission online). Prior experience serving on committees or participating in service-related activities. Research trajectory or agenda that would enhance departmental or university recognition via representation in journals and/or at conferences. Previous online teaching experience and/or using online learning platforms. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) professional-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $58,000 with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins November 2, 2026 ; position open until filled.?Please submit the following documents: A Cover Letter that highlights the candidate\u2019s interest in and qualification for the position. (no more than 2 pages, single spaced). We ask candidates to be both intentional and concise in identifying key strengths in your teaching, service and scholarship related to leadership and organizational communication. A Curriculum vitae A well-organized Effective Teaching Portfolio about the candidate\u2019s teaching experience, which may include a narrative of the candidate\u2019s pedagogical philosophy on student success, any quantitative/qualitative evidence of teaching effectiveness, a sample syllabus, and/or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness. (no page limit) A brief Research Statement about the candidate\u2019s scholarly expertise and future research trajectory (no more than 1 page, single spaced). Contact information for at least three professional references (including email addresses) Unofficial transcripts. Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Teaching Portfolio *Research Statement *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Ph.D. in Communication or related field, or are you ABD with a scheduled completion of degree by July 1, 2027, as indicated in the job posting. Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5499996/assistant-professor-of-communication": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Communication", "description": "Assistant Professor of Communication Salary $58,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC828-1 Division College of Humanities & Social Sciences Department Communication Opening Date 09/30/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Communication Department at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, seeks a nine-month full-time (tenure-track) Assistant Professor in the area of Communication Technology with an emphasis that connects the department\u2019s strengths in health communication, organizational communication, interpersonal communication, and digital media. We seek a colleague whose research and teaching engage at the intersection of communication and emerging technology including artificial intelligence, immersive technology, social media, and other forms of mediated communication. More information about the department and its programs can be found online at https://communication.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 credits per academic year (with potential for overload) in the Communication Department in areas of specialty. Provide regular institutional service as outlined in Regent and University policy. Adhere to department, college, and university policies and perform campus-wide faculty responsibilities, including: Holding office hours. Advising communication students. Attending department, division, and university meetings and events. Serving on university, college, and department committees. Engaging in community, university, departmental, and discipline service activities. Teach one or more courses per semester in online or blended formats. Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair and/or Dean. Qualifications A terminal degree in Communication or closely related discipline (A.B.D. considered). An active research trajectory or agenda that would enhance departmental or university recognition via representation in journals or at conferences. Experience teaching, and working with, students with diverse educational backgrounds. Previous online teaching experience and/or using online learning platforms such as Canvas, Moodle, or Blackboard. Demonstrated ability to integrate active learning and technology in the classroom. Grant writing and past work on grant funded projects a plus. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $58,000 with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins November 2, 2026 ; position open until filled.? Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a terminal degree by the first day of the semester in the required area(s) for this position, or are you ABD with a scheduled completion date of July 1, 2027 or earlier, as indicated in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5503641/assistant-professor-of-media-studies": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Media Studies", "description": "Assistant Professor of Media Studies Salary $58,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC841-1 Division College of Humanities & Social Sciences Department Communication Opening Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Communication at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, is seeking an enthusiastic and well-qualified individual for the position of Assistant Professor of Digital Media, with an emphasis in public relations and digital storytelling. The position requires a 4/4 teaching load, with instruction in the areas of public relations, social media, contemporary multimedia storytelling, cross-platform content creation and other courses as needed. The successful candidate will contribute to the Digital Media program while bringing depth in cross-platform strategic digital communication and content creation. The selected candidate will join a healthy and growing Communication Department. UT\u2019s polytechnic mission emphasizes a human-centered approach to problem-solving. As such, UT is particularly welcoming to active learning modalities in our coursework. Similarly, we encourage and value faculty scholarship that involves student researchers, as well as scholarship that informs the faculty member\u2019s teaching. More information about the department and its programs can be found online at https://communication.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach up to 24 credits annually with an emphasis on public relations and digital media storytelling plus the equivalent of 3 credit hours or more of institutional service as defined by the department and school. Course topics include public relations, strategic communication, cross-platform storytelling, digital content creation, and using media strategically to inform, persuade, and build relationships. Assist in the continuing growth of communication programs, with the ability and willingness to adapt courses to effectively utilize existing and developing instructional technology. Willing to become certified in online instruction and teach one or more courses online. Special preference will be given to candidates with experience in online teaching. Perform defined campus-wide faculty duties, including holding office hours, attendance at department and division meetings, and service on committees, with adherence to department, college, and university policies and procedures. Engage in scholarship and/or creative activity appropriate to a teaching university. UT values both scholarship of discovery and scholarship of pedagogy within the context of our teaching mission. Assist in mentoring, supervising, and assisting part-time instructors (adjunct faculty). Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Doctorate degree in Digital Media, Public Relations, or related field or MFA plus 10+ years of experience will also be considered. ABD will be considered if completion of degree will occur by July 1, 2027. Experience teaching and/or designing courses in digital media. Preference for candidates with expertise in digital media, digital communication, strategic digital media creation and management, public relations, digital storytelling, social media or related areas particularly as these areas intersect with contemporary public relations and strategic communication. Professional experience in public relations, digital media, social media, content strategy, or related fields is also preferred. Evidence of successful, student-centered teaching and with proficiency in instructional technology (finalists will complete a teaching demonstration to showcase competence). Ability to develop innovative curriculum and appropriate course content for face-to-face and online instruction. Eagerness and ability to engage with colleagues, staff and administrators to develop ways to improve the educational experience of Utah Tech students, both within communication and interdisciplinarily. Commitment to academic excellence, including utilizing computer-related technologies to enhance education methodology, and proficiency in curriculum design, program development, program evaluation, instruction, student guidance, and academic mentoring. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal skills. While teaching is the priority at UT, all tenure-track faculty at UT are expected to maintain a scholarly or creative agenda. We recognize and encourage diverse scholarly and creative pursuits. Faculty are free to pursue research, applied projects, or creative scholarship in the areas that inspire them, without being bound to a single methodological or topical focus. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $58,000 with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins November 9, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Doctorate degree in Digital Media, Public Relations, OR related field, or will you hold an MFA plus 10+ years of experience, OR are you ABD with a degree completion date of no later than July 1, 2027, as indicated in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5506329/biotechnology-program-lab-coordinator": {"title": "Biotechnology Program Lab Coordinator", "description": "Biotechnology Program Lab Coordinator Salary $55,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 27PRO619-2 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Biological Sciences Opening Date 10/06/2026 Closing Date 10/25/2026 11:59 PM Mountain Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Biotechnology Program at Utah Tech University (UT), within the Department of Biological Sciences, is launching three new programs in the 2026\u201327 academic year: the B.S. in Biotechnology, the BioLaunch program, and the M.S. in Genomics. We are seeking a year round, full-time Laboratory Coordinator to support laboratory operations across these programs. Key responsibilities include assisting BioLaunch student teams with lab access, experimental techniques, and project development, supporting faculty and students in Innovative-Based Learning laboratory courses, and maintaining cell culture lines used across all programs. The successful candidate will report to the Biotechnology program coordinator, collaborate with faculty, students, and industry partners to maintain a safe, well-equipped laboratory environment and ensure students have the training and resources needed for coursework and research success. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to the growth of new biotechnology program while preparing students for careers in biotechnology, biomedical research, and related fields. Additional information about the Department of Biological Sciences, faculty, and program offerings can be found at Utah Tech University Department of Biological Sciences. Responsibilities Cell Culture & Technical Support Maintain and expand cell lines (have to work during weekend as needed). Perform aseptic technique, passaging, cryopreservation, and thawing. Monitor and troubleshoot contamination (bacterial, fungal, mycoplasma). Support transfection, viral transduction, and other cell-based assays. Prepare media, reagents, and maintain cell culture documentation. Assist with experimental procedures including viability assays, microscopy, and molecular analyses. Laboratory Management Coordinate Laboratory operations in the biotechnology program with the support of faculty & other lab coordinators. Maintain supplies, lab ware, and instruments essential to the operation of BioLaunch and the Innovative-Based Learning lab(s). Maintain equipment including biosafety cabinets, CO2 incubators, centrifuges, and microscopes. Coordinate equipment maintenance and service schedules. Organize freezer storage and biological sample tracking. Keep accurate records and analyze and report relevant data. Develop and maintain standard operating procedures (SOPs). Other Work with department faculty to maintain a safe and productive laboratory environment. Attend department meetings; work with other faculty and staff in program management and adhere to university policies. Opportunity to Instruct select labs, with additional compensation. Work with Department Chair, Dean, Biotechnology program coordinator and other faculty in the Biological Sciences department on curriculum and program development. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor\u2019s degree in Biology or a closely related discipline from an accredited college or university, along with hands-on experience in mammalian cell culture, is required. A Master\u2019s degree in Biology or a closely related discipline from an accredited college or university is preferred. Teaching or training experience in a laboratory setting. Experience in cell culture techniques, particularly mammalian cell lines is preferred but not required. Experience with primary cells, stem cells, or 3D culture systems (preferred). Familiarity with safety standards and regulations as they pertain to biology laboratory work. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal skills. Willingness to work with and assist faculty and student teaching assistants. Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities. An eagerness to engage with colleagues, staff, and administrators to develop ways to improve the educational experience of UT students. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time, overtime-exempt staff position. Annual salary of $55,000 with a desired start date of January 2027. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, as well as paid holidays in addition to sick and vacation leave accruals. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 26, 2026 . Submit application materials (including resume contents and contact information for three professional references) and upload a cover letter electronically. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. Cover Letter Resume Contact information (including email) for three professional references Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold at least a Bachelor's degree and hands-on experience in the required area for this position by the desired start date? Yes No 03 Do you currently have teaching or training experience in a laboratory setting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5512881/support-specialist-for-occupational-therapy": {"title": "Support Specialist for Occupational Therapy", "description": "Support Specialist for Occupational Therapy Salary $40,000.00 - $42,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 27CLS945-2 Division College of Health Sciences Department Occupational Therapy Opening Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 10/25/2026 11:59 PM Mountain Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement Performs a variety of functions to support academic and administrative operations within the Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) program. This position will assist the Program Director in the processes involved with preparation of accreditation documents, managing various records and confidential information for faculty and students, meeting and event planning, monitoring existing programmatic efforts, fiscal/budget tracking, and other related duties. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, paired with a proactive and detail-oriented approach to work, will best serve the position. Additional information about the University can be found online at https://utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Serve as a central point liaison with other departments and external constituencies in coordinating a variety of day-to-day matters concerning the OTD program, including: Assist and resolve problems and inquiries of visitors. Review and control incoming and outgoing correspondence. Follow-up on operational commitments. Coordinate the scheduling of appointments and maintain calendars to support program needs, including facilities usage, events, catering, and travel arrangements. Oversee department budget management coordination, including submission of reimbursements, pay invoices, reconcile transactions, maintain expense records, and track department budgets. Provide resources to student queries (i.e. financial aid, counseling services) Assist in the preparation of internal and external reports and presentations, including accreditation, annual reports, and OTD program assessment by researching information, compiling statistics, and gathering various data. Track applicants for admission and selection into the OTD program, in close conjunction with the Graduate Studies Office, and coordinate with the Program Director to send acceptance and denial letters. Verify admission and program requirements for students are maintained throughout the program. Establish, update and maintain department files and confidential records. Provide software portal management for didactic, clinical, and capstone education, as well as curricular mapping, program learning outcomes, and accreditation needs. Manage and develop software operations for maintaining compliance with student requirements for program. In conjunction with UMAC and the Program Director, help to market the OTD Program. Assist in maintaining websites and social media applications. Prepare meeting agendas, as well as attend and take minutes for a variety of OTD Program meetings (as needed). Under the guidance of the Program Director, coordinate the onboarding of part-time administrative and clerical staff within the program. Coordinate continued website development and updates for OTD program to maintain compliance with accreditation and university standards/requirements. Coordinate faculty interview, hiring, and onboarding process for new full-time faculty. Perform other duties as assigned. Work may occasionally require flexible hours, including some weekend and evening hours for recruitment or related program events, etc. Qualifications Associate\u2019s degree, or equivalent level of college coursework, required. Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred. A combination of college coursework and work experience equivalent to four years will also be considered. At least two years\u2019 office experience required; experience working in higher education or specific administrative support staff experience preferred. The total qualifications required are based on a combination of education and work experience. Any experience used to meet the education requirement cannot also be used to meet the work experience requirement. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to learn quickly, be creative, work independently, set priorities, and meet deadlines. Must be well organized and able to function well in a changing environment and enjoy the administrative challenges of working with several initiatives, as well as being attentive to detail. Ability to interact with administrators, faculty, staff, and students at all levels while in a fast-paced, evolving environment, remaining proactive and efficient, with a high level of professionalism. Ability to diplomatically handle complex situations involving competing interests and priorities during periods of high volume and frequent interruptions. Demonstrated ability to develop and maintain financial records, budgets, and various databases. Strong computer skills in the Microsoft Office Suite (specifically word processing, spreadsheets, and email), desktop publishing, library and web-based research, and email. Experience updating and maintain websites and social media applications, as well as Google application and experience in using a Learning Management System preferred. Ability to quickly learn organization-specific and other computer application programs, such as EXXAT, OTCAS, Zoom, and Qualtrics. Excellent written and oral communication skills; demonstrated ability of English grammar, punctuation, and correspondence forms. Skill in exercising discretion and managing confidential records and information. Demonstrated ability to perform general office practices and procedures, including office machines, inventory, ordering, etc. Excellent customer service and support-oriented skills in interacting with administrators, faculty, staff, and students. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time overtime-exempt executive staff position. Annual salary of $40,000-$42,000 depending on qualifications and experience. Desired start date by January 2027. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, as well as paid holidays in addition to sick and vacation leave accruals. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 26, 2026 . Submit application materials (including resume contents and contact information for three professional references) and upload a cover letter electronically. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https:/