important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. Cover Letter Resume Contact information (including email) for three professional references Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold at least a Bachelor's or master's degree in accounting by the desired start date? Yes No 03 Do you currently have at least five (5) years of accounting experience? CPA certification may be substituted for up to three (3) years of experience. The total qualifications required are based on a combination of education and work experience. Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5442313/assistant-professor-of-occupational-therapy": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Occupational Therapy", "description": "Assistant Professor of Occupational Therapy Salary $80,000.00 - $90,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC699-1 Division College of Health Sciences Department Occupational Therapy Opening Date 08/10/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The new Occupational Therapy Doctoral (OTD) Program in the College of Health Sciences at Utah Tech University in St. George, Utah, seeks a doctoral-prepared occupational therapist to join an innovative team of instructors within the University\u2019s new Occupational Therapy program, in compliance with ACOTE educational standards. The successful candidate will develop and teach graduate level occupational therapy courses, with priority selection given to those applicants with expertise in mental health, children and youth, and adult or older adult practice experience. In addition, the successful candidate will engage in student advisement and service to the University. All OTD faculty develop an agenda relative to research and/or scholarly activity for potential student research mentorship and involvement. Faculty members exemplify the teacher-practitioner-investigator model by following excellent teaching practices, scholarly activity, and professional behaviors consistent with the mission of Utah Tech University. This is a 10.5-month faculty position, with a desired start date of Fall 2026 (initial workload will be non-instructional in course development until teaching can begin). More information about the college, faculty, and degree offerings can be found online at https://health.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Serve as course director and maintain currency with health care trends, research, and OT practice, especially as it relates to area of expertise. Provide evaluations that are appropriate, equitable, and professional, and that provide constructive feedback to the student. Exhibit objectivity in all dealings with students and in all aspects of the learning process. Continually adapt teaching strategies in the implementation of the course to meet the needs of all students. Treat confidential information about students, colleagues and others with fairness, discretion and integrity. Develop and maintain proficiency in teaching areas through investigation, formal education, continuing education, and/or practice. Participate in evaluation of teaching methods and curriculum, and modify both in response to feedback. Serve as academic advisor for students in the OT program or interested in the program, as designated. Serve as doctoral experience/capstone project mentor, as appropriate. Supervise student graduate research projects, as appropriate. Contribute to the advancement of OT through research, practice, and/or service. Pursue opportunities to publish/present occupational therapy/research activities. Assist with clinical instruction of students, as appropriate. Participate in the University governance and/or occupational therapy department, College of Health Sciences, committees. Carry out assigned duties with punctuality and professional competence. Except in cases of emergency, shall not be absent from their assigned teaching or other assignments without first informing the Program Director, Department Chair, or the appropriate administrator. Maintain active membership in state and national professional associations. Collaborate in and contribute to the preparation of academic reports and accreditation self-studies. Prepare and implement a faculty development plan annually. Perform defined faculty duties, including holding office hours, attendance at department and division meetings, and adherence to college, division, and university policies and procedures. Provide regular institutional service as outlined in regent and university policies. Work collaboratively with the Chair, Program Director, faculty, and staff to ensure compliance with department, program, and ACOTE standards. Perform other duties, as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Certification by NBCOT as OTR. Possess a doctoral degree from a USDE-recognized regionally accredited institution. The doctoral degree is not limited to a doctorate in occupational therapy. Must be licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the state of Utah. Minimum of three years of professional practice experience. Intermediate to advanced clinical skills in the primary area of teaching. Skilled in application of research and evidence-based practices to new environments. Knowledge, skills and mindset as a creator and/or innovator and/or entrepreneur. Superior written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills needed for working with diverse stakeholders. Proficient with computer technology and strong organization, problem-solving, and counseling skills. Current member of the Utah Occupational Therapy Association Current member of the American Occupational Therapy Association Preferred Qualifications: Experience in academic program or curricular development and knowledge of ACOTE standards. Teaching experience at the college/university level. Experience with online teaching. Experience in scholarly activity. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (10.5-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service begins Fall 2026. Annual salary of $80,000-$90,000 depending on qualifications and experience. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins September 14, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY:? Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Doctoral degree by the first day of the semester in the required area(s) for this position from a USDE-recognized regionally accredited institution, as indicated in the job posting? The doctoral degree is not limited to a doctorate in occupational therapy. Yes No 03 Do you currently have at least three years of experience as listed in the job announcement? Yes No 04 Do you currently hold the required certification by NBCOT as OTR, and are you licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the state of Utah? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5442367/assistant-professor-of-exercise-science": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science", "description": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science Salary $61,000.00 - $66,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC781-1 Division College of Health Sciences Department Health & Human Performance Opening Date 08/10/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Health and Human Performance at Utah Tech University in St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty position in Exercise Science to start January 2027 (Spring Semester; preferred) or July 2027 (Fall Semester). This position directly supports the Exercise Science degree programs, which include pre-Physical Therapy (PT), pre-Occupational Therapy (OT), and pre-Athletic Training (AT) emphases. Candidates with a specialization in Sport and Exercise Psychology, Motor Development, and Exercise Programming for Special or At-Risk Populations are preferred but consideration will be given to all qualified applicants. More information about the department, faculty, and its degree offerings can be found online at https://health.utahtech.edu/health-human-performance/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 credits per academic year, primarily in-person, but with online teaching options. Instruction may include a combination of classroom/lab teaching and/or internship supervision. Courses may include but are not limited to Sport and Exercise Psychology, Motor Development, Exercise Programming for At-Risk Populations, Applied Fitness Development for Older Adults, and other Exercise Science related courses. Design curriculum and create student experiences/internships reflective of the University\u2019s theme \"active learning. active life.\" Hold regular office hours, attend regular department meetings, vote on department issues, and advise on student assessment as needed. Serve on University, college, and department committees and engage in community, University, departmental, program, and professional discipline service activities. Engage in scholarly and creative activities resulting in the sharing of knowledge through teaching, presentations, publications, and other appropriate outlets. Develop and maintain supporting relationships with community, state, national, and international organizations. Advise and prepare students for credentialing licensure exams through ACSM, NSCA, etc. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Doctorate degree in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, or a related field required. ABD candidates will be considered. Candidates with a specialization or degree in Sports Psychology or Motor Development is preferred. Evidence of or potential for excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels (finalists will be required to demonstrate competence via a teaching demonstration). Evidence of clinical or sport performance work-related experience in exercise science is strongly preferred. Ability to communicate clearly with students, staff and colleagues, both orally and in writing. Ability to develop collaborative relationships with faculty and administrators across disciplines and with other members of discipline-related external organizations. Evidence of scholarship in the form of refereed publications, paper presentations, published abstracts, etc. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits starting January 1 (preferred) or July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $61,000-$66,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins Monday, 14 September ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Doctoral degree or are you ABD, as indicated in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5463745/instructor-of-the-practice-in-engineering-labs": {"title": "Instructor of the Practice in Engineering Labs", "description": "Instructor of the Practice in Engineering Labs Salary See Position Description Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC701-1 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Engineering Opening Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Announcement The College of Science, Engineering, and Technology at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time Instructor of the Practice in Engineering Labs position to begin Spring Semester (January 2027). Come join an active group of educators dedicated to offering students immersive experiences with lab courses, facilitating UTXplore projects, and equipment training. More information about the Engineering Department can be found online at https://mech.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 30 credits of laboratory and/or lecture courses in the Engineering Department each academic year. Maintain labs and lab equipment within the Engineering Department. Ensure engineering labs are compliant with university, state, and federal safety regulations. Provide prototyping guidance to students involved in UTXplore, capstone, design practicum, and research projects. Attend department, college, and division faculty meetings; work with other faculty in program management and adhere to University policy and procedures. Perform defined campus-wide duties, including holding office hours, functioning as an advisor to students, and performing university service and scholarship as defined by academic policy. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications M.S. in an engineering discipline, or related field, required. Candidates with a B.S. degree in an engineering discipline that have relevant work experience and/or a M.S. degree in a non-related field will also be considered. Relevant industry experience is preferred. Familiarity with equipment, whether machining, controllers, or electronic testing equipment, is preferred. A strong manufacturing and prototyping background is preferred. Prior teaching experience in engineering or related courses preferred. A strong commitment to and evidence of potential for excellence in teaching. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a commitment to collegiality and teamwork. An interest in active learning, experiential learning, and student engagement is desirable. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) professional-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits begins January 1, 2027. Annual salary of $83,000-$86,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins September 28, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7520. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5463779/instructor-of-the-practice-or-assistant-professor-of-physics": {"title": "Instructor of the Practice or Assistant Professor of Physics", "description": "Instructor of the Practice or Assistant Professor of Physics Salary See Position Description Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC924-1 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Engineering Opening Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Announcement The Engineering Department within the College of Science, Engineering, and Technology at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor or Instructor of the Practice of Physics to begin Spring Semester (January 2027). Come join an active group of educators dedicated to offering students immersive experiences. More information about the Engineering Department can be found online at https://mech.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 credits (Assistant Professor) or 30 credits (Instructor of the Practice) of lecture and/or laboratory courses annually. Perform defined campus-wide duties, including holding office hours, functioning as an advisor to students, and performing university service and scholarship as defined by academic policy. Attend department, college, and division faculty meetings; work with other faculty in program management and adhere to University policy and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum of an Ph.D. in Physics or related field (Assistant Professor) or M.S. in Physics or related field (Instructor of the Practice). Candidates with a B.S. in Physics or related field that have relevant industry experience and/or a M.S. degree in a non-related field will also be considered. Teaching experience with demonstrated ability of successful teaching including laboratory experience preferred. Demonstrated ability to work well with other faculty, staff and students. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) professional-track or tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service, with pay and benefits begins January 1, 2027. Annual salary of $58,000-$61,000 for Instructor of the Practice, and $64,000-$67,000 for Assistant Professor depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins September 28, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5468561/assistant-professor-of-geology": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Geology", "description": "Assistant Professor of Geology Salary $63,000.00 - $66,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC847-1 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Earth & Environmental Sciences Opening Date 09/01/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences at Utah Tech University in St. George, UT, invites applications for a Geology position to begin January 2027 (Spring Semester; preferred) or July 2027 (Fall Semester). The focus of the position is on structural geology, tectonics, field geology, and related areas. The selected candidate will teach courses at the general education through upper division level within their specialty, as well as mentor undergraduate research projects, which are required for graduation. Candidates should possess a Ph.D. in Geology or closely related field. The successful candidate will teach courses and be expected to contribute to the continued growth of the program. More information about the department, faculty, and its degree offerings can be found online at https://ees.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 credits of lecture and laboratory courses each academic year. Teach undergraduate courses in geology and related fields, with a focus on structural geology, tectonics, and field geology. Supervise undergraduate research projects, fostering a supportive academic environment and the application of skills learned in the classroom. Collaborate with faculty within the department and across disciplines to enhance interdisciplinary research and education initiatives. Provide instructional support for the department\u2019s field school as needed. Participate in departmental, college, university, and community service. Develop innovative course materials and teaching methods to enhance student learning and engagement. Mentor and support students in their academic and professional development. Contribute to curriculum development and program assessment within the department. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Geology, Earth Sciences, Geography, or a closely related field by the start date. A record of expertise in structural geology and tectonics, evidenced by publications and/or grant funding. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness at the undergraduate level. Ability to engage with students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Postdoctoral experience preferred. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting January 1 (preferred) or July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $63,000-$66,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 5, 2026 ; position open until filled.? Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a Doctoral degree by the first day of the semester in the required area(s) for this position, as indicated in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5479224/instructor-of-the-practice-or-assistant-professor-in-cybersecurity": {"title": "Instructor of the Practice or Assistant Professor in Cybersecurity", "description": "Instructor of the Practice or Assistant Professor in Cybersecurity Salary $73,000.00 - $94,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC682-1 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Computing Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Announcement The Department of Computing at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, invites applicants for a full-time professional-track Instructor of the Practice or Assistant Professor in Cybersecurity, starting July 1, 2027. We are seeking someone that has a strong knowledge of SCADA and ICS security and that can complement our existing expertise. More information about the department, faculty, and its degree offerings can be found online at https://catalog.utahtech.edu/programs/computing/ . Responsibilities For Instructor of the Practice - teach 30 credits of lecture and laboratory courses in cybersecurity each academic year. For Assistant Professor \u2013 teach 24 credits of lecture and laboratory courses in cybersecurity each academic year. Contribute to the ongoing development of programs and projects in Cybersecurity and related areas. Perform defined campus-wide duties including holding office hours, attending department, college, and division faculty meetings, and adhering to University policy and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications To be considered for the Instructor of the Practice a Master\u2019s degree in Cybersecurity or closely related field by Spring 2027 is required. A terminal degree in Cybersecurity, IT, Engineering, Computer Science, or related field is required to be considered for the Assistant Professor. Industry experience strongly preferred. Interest in Industrial Control Systems security preferred. Prior teaching experience is a plus. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a commitment to collegiality and teamwork are desired. An interest in active learning, experiential learning, and student engagement is also desirable. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) professional-track or tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $73,000 - $77,000 for Instructor of the Practice or $90,000 - $94,000 for Assistant Professor with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026 ; position open until filled. ?Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5479237/assistant-professor-of-marketing": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing", "description": "Assistant Professor of Marketing Salary $100,000.00 - $106,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC676-1 Division College of Business Department Management & Marketing Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Management and Marketing at Utah Tech University in St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Marketing with a primary specialization in Product Marketing. In alignment with Utah Tech University's polytechnic mission, this tenure track faculty member will expand and enhance applied, industry-engaged learning in how organizations develop, position, differentiate, launch, manage, and grow products and brands. The position will emphasize the integration of customer insight, innovation, technology, and real-world marketing practice to prepare students for contemporary careers in product marketing and related fields. The successful candidate will contribute to the Marketing program through teaching, research, student mentoring, and engagement with industry and the broader community. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong combination of academic scholarship and professional industry experience in product marketing or closely related areas, such as product strategy, new product development, go-to-market strategy, technology commercialization, innovation, product lifecycle management, positioning, differentiation, market adoption, and customer insight. Candidates should have an active research agenda that contributes to the academic literature in product marketing or a closely related field, as well as meaningful professional experience applying these concepts in organizational settings. Professional or research experience in brand strategy and/or brand management is valued as a complement to product marketing expertise. The Utah Tech Marketing program offers a marketing BA/BS major with career-focused areas of study in Digital Marketing, Marketing Analytics, Hospitality and Services Marketing, and General Marketing, as well as a marketing minor and certificates. More information about the department, faculty, and degree offerings can be found at https://marketing.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach and design 24 credit hours of lower- and/or upper-division courses per academic year across different delivery modalities. Courses could include Product Marketing, Marketing Strategy, Principles of Marketing, Entrepreneurial Marketing, and new upper-division electives related to product strategy, go-to-market execution, product positioning, technology marketing, innovation, or related areas. Advise undergraduate marketing students, mentor student projects, and contribute to experiential learning opportunities and industry-engaged activities. Provide institutional and campus service as defined by University Policy and the College of Business, including holding office hours, attending department and College of Business meetings and committee service in compliance with university policy. Maintain an active program of scholarly research and publication consistent with the expectations for tenure and promotion at Utah Tech University. Qualifications PhD or DBA in Marketing from an AACSB-accredited institution required; candidates who are ABD will be considered if the degree will be completed by August 2027. Active research agenda with evidence of scholarly productivity in product marketing or a closely related area, such as product management, new product development, product lifecycle management, product or marketing strategy, go-to-market strategy, positioning and differentiation, technology commercialization, innovation, market adoption or diffusion, customer insight or co-creation, portfolio strategy, emerging marketing technologies, or related areas. Demonstrated professional industry experience in product marketing, product management, go-to-market strategy and/or execution, product strategy, technology commercialization, or a closely related area is required. Demonstrated ability to design innovative, applied curriculum and deliver engaging instruction. Finalists will be required to deliver a teaching demonstration. Strong written and oral communication skills, with a proven ability to collaborate effectively within a team-oriented environment. Experience working with industry partners and incorporating experiential, project-based, or technology-enhanced learning into the classroom is preferred. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $100,000-$106,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, employee assistance and wellness programs, life, disability, retirement, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a one- to two-page statement describing their current and future research agenda, statement of teaching philosophy/effectiveness,contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), and transcripts. Semifinalists may be asked for a representative research paper/working paper. Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. If, because of a disability, you need special services or facilities to apply for this opening, please call the Human Resources Office (435) 652-7520. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a PhD or DBA in Marketing or are you ABD with a projected completion date prior to 1 August 2027, as indicated in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5479297/assistant-professor-of-computational-biology": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Computational Biology", "description": "Assistant Professor of Computational Biology Salary $80,000.00 - $86,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC667-1 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Biological Sciences Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Biological Sciences at Utah Tech University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Computational Biology, with a primary focus on Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) algorithms and their pedagogical application at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. This position is part of a two-position hire supporting the department's expanding programs in bioinformatics and genomics. The successful candidate will be an expert in NGS algorithms and pipeline development, capable of translating complex computational concepts for students at varying levels of experience. The position will provide instruction for an existing Bachelor of Science in Bioinformatics and Master of Science in Genomics with a Bioinformatics emphasis. The Biological Sciences department houses degree programs in Bioinformatics, Biological Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, Natural Sciences, and Biology Secondary Education. Additional program information is available at https://biology.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teaching and Curriculum Teach 24 credit hours of lower and/or upper-division courses per academic year across undergraduate and graduate levels. Deliver upper-division and master's-level courses in NGS algorithms, bioinformatics pipeline design, computational genomics, and related topics, with the ability to adapt instruction to students from both computational and life science backgrounds. Teach core NGS topics including short- and long-read sequencing platforms, read alignment algorithms (e.g., BWA, STAR, minimap2), variant calling, de novo assembly, transcriptomics, and epigenomics analysis. Develop and teach additional courses as needed, which may include Principles of Genetics, Introduction to Programming for Biologists, or Statistical Genomics, depending on departmental need and applicant expertise. Create innovative upper-level elective courses that reflect emerging areas of NGS technology and computational biology, complementing and diversifying the department's current offerings. Design and deliver instruction in multiple modalities including face-to-face, flipped classroom, hybrid, and fully online formats; willingness to teach evening and summer courses when needed. Research and Mentorship Mentor master's students in functional genomics and NGS-focused research projects, guiding them from data generation through computational analysis and interpretation. Supervise undergraduate research in computational biology, providing hands-on experience with NGS datasets and bioinformatics workflows. Maintain an active scholarly profile consistent with the teacher-scholar model, including publications, presentations, or collaborative research appropriate to a primarily undergraduate and master's serving institution. Assist in mentoring and supervising part-time instructors teaching in the bioinformatics program. Service and Institutional Contribution Collaborate with the Department Chair, Dean, and faculty colleagues on curriculum development, program assessment, and strategic planning for both the Bioinformatics B.S. and Genomics M.S. programs. Perform campus-wide service duties including holding regular office hours, attending department and division meetings, serving on university and college committees, and participating in outreach and recruitment activities. Contribute to interdisciplinary curricular and scholarly activities within the Department, the College of Science, Engineering & Technology, and the University. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required PhD in Computational Biology, Bioinformatics, Genomics, Computer Science with a biological application focus, or a closely related field. Demonstrated expertise in NGS algorithms and the analysis of high-throughput sequencing data, with proficiency in at least one scripting/programming language (Python, R, Bash, or equivalent) and familiarity with bioinformatics tools and workflow management systems (e.g., Snakemake, Nextflow). Successful teaching experience at the college or university level, with evidence of effective instruction of NGS and computational biology topics to students from diverse disciplinary backgrounds. Demonstrated ability to design and deliver innovative curriculum using a variety of instructional approaches, including active learning, project-based learning, and computational lab environments. Commitment to inclusive excellence: ability to work respectfully and collaboratively with students and colleagues from all backgrounds, and demonstrated advocacy for women, people of color, first-generation students, and other groups underrepresented in computational sciences. Strong written and oral communication skills, including the ability to explain complex algorithmic concepts clearly to non-expert audiences. Demonstrated capacity for continuous professional development, including staying current with rapidly evolving NGS technologies, tools, and best practices. Preferred Postdoctoral or industry experience applying NGS methods in a research context. Experience teaching or mentoring in a bioinformatics, genomics, or data science program at the graduate level. Familiarity with cloud computing environments (AWS, Google Cloud, or equivalent) and high-performance computing clusters for large-scale genomics analyses and workflow management tools (Nextflow, Snakemake). Experience developing online or hybrid bioinformatics courses, including the design of computational lab modules and auto-graded assessments. Track record of interdisciplinary collaboration bridging computational and experimental biology. Strong commitment to the teacher-scholar model at a primarily undergraduate institution (PUI). Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting 1 January 2027. Annual salary of $80,000-$86,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026 ; position open until filled.? Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Do you hold a PhD in Computational Biology, Bioinformatics, Genomics, Computer Science with a biological application focus, or a closely related field, as required in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5479425/assistant-professor-of-biology": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Biology", "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Salary $60,000.00 - $66,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC684-1 Division College of Science, Engineering & Technology Department Biological Sciences Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Biological Sciences a at Utah Tech University in St. George, UT invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position with a focus on Wildlife Management and Conservation. This position is well-suited for a seasoned professional scientist dedicated to teaching lecture and laboratory courses at a primarily undergraduate institution that emphasizes excellent in teaching and research. More information about the Department and its associated programs and faculty can be found online at https://biology.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach 24 credits of lower division lecture and laboratory courses each academic year, including upper division courses in applicant\u2019s area of expertise as well as introductory and general education courses. Collaborate with other full-time faculty on curriculum development of both lab and lecture courses to ensure similar learning core themes, and assist/mentor part-time instructors as needed. Coordinate select lab courses, including overseeing lab set-up and take down, ordering of supplies, and supervision of lab instructors. Attend department, division, and college faculty meetings. Work with other faculty in program management. Adhere to university policies. Involve undergraduate students in research and experiential-learning projects in applicant's area of expertise, as time permits. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications PhD in Biology, Environmental Science, or closely related discipline from an accredited college of university required. Experience with geospatial technology or conservation and resource management preferred. Professional background in laboratory management, laboratory research, etc. preferred. Evidence of potential for successful teaching at the college level required. Strong written, verbal and interpersonal skills. Willingness to work with and assist part-time instructors. An eagerness to engage with colleagues, staff and administrators to develop ways to improve the educational experience for our students. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting January 2027. Annual salary of $60,000-$66,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 19, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted. *Cover Letter *Curriculum Vitae *Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses) *Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) *Student Success Statement Have you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a PhD in the required area for this position by the desired start date? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5435375/assistant-professor-of-elementary-education": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Elementary Education", "description": "Assistant Professor of Elementary Education Salary $60,000.00 - $65,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC668-1 Division College of Education Department Teacher Education Opening Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Position Announcement The Department of Education at Utah Tech University (UT) in St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position, specializing in Elementary Education, starting Spring or Fall Semester 2027. The goal of the UT Education Department is to prepare its students to be outstanding teachers within diverse and changing communities through the integration of leadership, scholarship, reflection, and community partnerships. The UT Education Department offers two top-performing pre-service teacher preparation programs with stable enrollment, and faculty in the Department collaborate closely to support student success. More information about the department and its programs can be found online at https://education.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach specialized pedagogy classes in one or more of the following areas: literacy, social studies methods, differentiation, teaching multilingual learners, classroom assessment, curriculum and lesson planning Teach general pedagogy courses for the Elementary Education program. Assist in the development of new curriculum and programs. Assist in meeting requirements of national accreditation, as well as USBE state licensure competencies Work with local school district personnel to ensure the UT Elementary Education program successfully prepares students to teach at the elementary level. Supervise and mentor students in field experience settings. Fulfill faculty responsibilities including holding office hours, advising students, attending faculty and other University meetings, and serving on university, college, and department committees. Provide regular institutional service as outlined in Regent and University policy. Adhere to department, college, and university policies. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Doctoral degree in Teacher Education, Elementary Education, or related field required. Applicants who are advanced ABD candidates will also be considered if degree completion will occur prior to the hire date. A Deep knowledge of The Science of Reading and expertise in the area of literacy. Ability to work collaboratively with others to maintain cohesion of the elementary education program. Experience teaching college level literacy courses and/or graduate courses preferred. LETRS training preferred, or willingness to be trained within 60 days of hire. Minimum of five (5) years' experience teaching students in grades K-6 preferred Demonstrated ability in successful teaching of college students. Finalists will be required to demonstrate competence through a teaching demonstration. Demonstrated ability and interest in creative, unique, and effective approaches to teacher education. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, both orally and in writing. Good organizational and time management skills. Candidates must have excellent knowledge and skills with technology, including online instruction. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service begins either 1 January or 1 July 2027. Annual salary of $60,000-$65,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins September 8, 2026 ; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), transcripts, and a Student Success Statement (1-2 pages about the candidate\u2019s teaching or other professional experience working with a wide range of student academic preparedness). Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University\u2019s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University\u2019s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply"}}, "rows": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492866/assistant-professor-of-english": {"school_id": 1447, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492866/assistant-professor-of-english", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of English", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of English", "area_key_words": "English; Rhetoric", "deadline_of_application": "October 26, 2026", "position_start_date": "July 1, 2027"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492917/assistant-professor-of-psychology-marriage-and-family-therapy": {"school_id": 1447, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492917/assistant-professor-of-psychology-marriage-and-family-therapy", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of Psychology - Marriage and Family Therapy", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Psychology", "deadline_of_application": "October 26, 2026", "position_start_date": "January 1, 2027"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492976/resident-life-area-coordinator": {"school_id": 1447, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5492976/resident-life-area-coordinator", "job_title_in_post": "Resident Life Area Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "departmen